# reckoner — .gitignore
#
# The rule this file exists to enforce: **build output is ignored, records are
# not.** The chess campaign learned it four separate times, each time by hand
# after the fact — a BLOCKED.md ignored outright, a bare `data/` that stopped git
# descending into runs/data/, benchmarks/results.jsonl silently unversioned, and
# runs/** swallowing ANCHORS.sha256 on the very commit that added it. Every
# negation below is therefore written *before* the run that produces the file it
# names, and tests/test_gitignore_musttrack.py is the judge — `git check-ignore`
# answers for hypothetical paths, so a rule can be tested the day it is written.

# --- run artifacts ---------------------------------------------------------
# Checkpoints and datasets are far too large to track. The exceptions are the
# small provenance and narrative files a campaign log cites as evidence.
# `!runs/**/` lets git descend into the tree to reach them.
runs/**
!runs/**/
# The Phase 2 loop's only durable narrative — ~50 rows for a 24h run, and
# nothing else survives the process.
!runs/**/iterations.jsonl
# The ladder log is the *verdict*. In the chess campaign it was ignored, and
# every file the RUNLOG cited as evidence would have failed to enter the repo.
!runs/**/ladder.jsonl
!runs/**/ladder_diagnostic.jsonl
!runs/**/ladder_pairscores.jsonl
# `pair_scores` is persisted from the first ladder row (inherited law), so its
# negation exists from the first commit rather than from the first pass.
!runs/**/metrics.jsonl
# A run's *resolved* config is what makes its rows reproducible; the campaign
# reads this copy, not configs/. Same for the SHA + fingerprint pair.
!runs/**/config.yaml
!runs/**/provenance.json
!runs/**/meta.json
# Perturbations carry their cause: annotations.jsonl explains blips in a run's
# own timing series, keyed by iteration, so iterations.jsonl can be read six
# weeks out without reconstructing why one row is slow.
!runs/**/annotations.jsonl
# The value-head switch event log — every evaluation writes, INCLUDING the ones
# that abstain. An abstention nobody records is indistinguishable from a
# criterion nobody ran.
!runs/**/value_switch.jsonl
# The resume commit marker: the only artifact that makes an iteration real.
!runs/**/LATEST
!runs/**/state-*.json
# Dataset and suite digests — the anchor list the whole campaign is measured
# against (plan chunk 5).
!runs/ANCHORS.sha256
# The frozen suites ARE the measuring stick (chunk 5). ~1.2K problems, a few
# hundred KB of JSONL, and every number the campaign ever reports is measured
# against them — a suite git silently dropped makes the whole ladder
# unreproducible. The memmap arrays beside them stay ignored: those are bulk,
# rebuildable from the seed, and the meta.json carries their digests.
!runs/suites/*.jsonl
# The ladder's PAIRED SETS are the same species as the suites: frozen at birth,
# digested into ANCHORS, and the thing every ladder number is measured against.
# A paired set git drops makes every pass ever run on it unreproducible, and
# unlike a dataset it cannot be regenerated — regenerating it makes a different
# instrument. `pairedset.freeze` asserts its own trackedness before writing.
!runs/paired/*.jsonl
# The two-level contamination censuses. The decision rule is pre-stated; these are
# the arithmetic it was applied to, and a dropped candidate list nobody can read is
# a census nobody ran. A GLOB, not the one filename: the exact negation shipped
# first and `paired_census_postfreeze.json` hit the guard on the very next write —
# the same "widen to the class" lesson as runs/gate_*.json, met once more.
!runs/paired_census*.json
# Chunk-11 Part 0's headroom measurement and the ceiling arithmetic derived from it.
!runs/chunk11_*.json
# The test count, WRITTEN BY THE RUN rather than typed into a commit message.
# F-16's rule ("compose the message after the run") broke one commit after it was
# written, because message and run are convenient to send together and a rule that
# fights convenience loses. A number nobody types cannot be a number nobody
# measured. Carries `whole_suite` so a targeted run's total cannot read as a full
# one — the same failure in a new costume.
!runs/testcount.json
# Instrument outputs that later chunks cite as evidence.
!runs/rule_participation.json
!runs/state_extent.json
!runs/par_delta.json
!runs/suite_verification.json
# Gate records: the arithmetic a gate was DECLARED on, and the table a gate was
# re-run into. These three shipped untracked in chunks 7-8 — cited as evidence by
# a report, matched by `runs/**`, and missed by the guard because a rule that is
# never written is never tested (ERRATA-chunk7.md §5). The pattern is deliberately
# a glob: the next gate record is covered the day it is written, not after.
!runs/gate_*.json
!runs/chunk*_gate_table.json
# Pre-flight projections. F-03 is on record because a projection was wrong by 5x
# and the estimate had not been kept; a projection that is not saved cannot be
# scored against the run it projected.
!runs/pilot_*.json
!runs/shakedown_*.json
# Contamination censuses. Each is a gate's evidence, pinned to the digests it was
# computed against, and A1 made them a standing obligation rather than a one-off.
!runs/*contamination*.json
!runs/*independence*.json
!runs/gpu_*.json
# Per-run records: the result a run reported, and the environment it ran in. The
# checkpoint beside them stays ignored — it is bulk, and its provenance travels
# in its own meta.
!runs/**/*_result.json
!runs/**/check_env.txt
!runs/**/anchor.json

# Root-scoped: a bare `data/` would also swallow runs/data/ as a *directory*
# ignore, and git cannot descend into an ignored directory to reach the
# negations above.
/data/

# --- benchmarks ------------------------------------------------------------
# Deliberately NOT ignored, and this comment is the reason. benchmarks/ holds
# bench scripts *and* results.jsonl — a dated, SHA-stamped record. A
# `benchmarks/**` rule with a negation for results.jsonl would have ignored
# every future bench script instead, which is the same mistake in the other
# direction. Nothing here is build output.

# --- build / env -----------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.py[co]
*.pt
*.npy
*.dat
*.egg-info/
dist/
build/
.venv/
# uv.lock is deliberately NOT ignored. Without it committed, a clean-clone gate
# tests today's resolution luck rather than reproducibility: `make install`
# would re-resolve every dependency at whatever versions exist that morning, and
# "green in a clean clone" would silently mean "green against a different
# environment than the one the numbers were measured on". `make install` runs
# `uv sync --frozen`, and `make lint` runs `uv lock --check`, so the lockfile
# and pyproject.toml cannot drift apart unnoticed.
.ruff_cache/
.pytest_cache/
*.ipynb_checkpoints/

# Review bundles zipped for external review (regenerable)
*.zip

# Machine-local Claude Code settings (and the atomic-write temp files it leaves)
.claude/settings.local.json*
*.tmp.*
